{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"In general, to find the derivative (i.e. the expression for $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}$ ) of a function defined parametrically by the equations $x=u(t)$ and $y=v(t)$ (where $u$ and $v$ are any functions of $t$), we use the following rule:\n\n$\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\\dfrac{\\left(\\dfrac{dy}{dt}\\right)}{\\left(\\dfrac{dx}{dt}\\right)}=\\dfrac{v'(t)}{u'(t)}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"We are given that $x=\\sqrt{1-3t}$ and $y=\\dfrac{3}{t}$:\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\\dfrac{dy}{dx}\u0026=\\dfrac{\\dfrac{d}{dt}\\left(\\dfrac{3}{t}\\right)}{\\dfrac{d}{dt}(\\sqrt{1-3t})}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{\\left(-\\dfrac{3}{t^2}\\right)}{\\left(-\\dfrac{3}{2\\sqrt{1-3t}}\\right)}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{2\\sqrt{1-3t}}{t^2}\\qquad\\gray{\\text{Simplify}}\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Now let's evaluate $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}$ at $t=\\blueD {-1}$:\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}\\dfrac{2\\sqrt{1-3(\\blueD{-1})}}{(\\blueD{-1})^2}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{2\\cdot 2}{1}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=4\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In conclusion, the value of $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}$ at $t=-1$ is $4$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"A curve in the plane is defined parametrically by the equations $x=\\sqrt{1-3t}$ and $y=\\dfrac{3}{t}$.\n\n**Find the value of $\\dfrac{dy}{dx}$ at $t=-1$.**\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$4$","correct":true},{"content":"$-3$","correct":false},{"content":"$-12$","isNoneOfTheAbove":false},{"content":"$2$","isNoneOfTheAbove":false}],"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":false,"multipleSelect":false,"onePerLine":false,"randomize":true},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
